            <h1>Dr. Lydia Moreno</h1>
            <p class="lead">Associate Professor of Computational Neuroscience at Riverbend University’s School of Biological Sciences.</p>
            <p>My research develops interpretable machine-learning methods to understand how neural circuits encode sensory information, with applications spanning two-photon imaging, connectomics, and single-cell omics.</p>
            <div class="hero-actions" aria-label="Profile links">
              <a class="button" href="publications.html">View Publications</a>
              <a class="button secondary" href="mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu">Contact Me</a>
            </div>
          </div>
          <aside class="profile-card" aria-label="Contact information">
            <div class="avatar" aria-hidden="true">LM</div>
            <h2>Research Profile</h2>
            <ul class="contact-list">
              <li><strong>Email:</strong> <a href="mailto:lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu">lydia.moreno@riverbend.edu</a></li>
              <li><strong>Office:</strong> Blakely Hall, Room 312, Riverbend University</li>
              <li><strong>Twitter:</strong> <a href="https://twitter.com/LydiaNeuroLab">@LydiaNeuroLab</a></li>
              <li><strong>GitHub:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/lydia-moreno">github.com/lydia-moreno</a></li>
            </ul>
          </aside>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="about-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">About Me</p>
          <h2 id="about-title">Decoding neural systems with transparent computational tools</h2>
        </div>
        <p>Dr. Moreno received her Ph.D. in Computational Biology from Baywood Institute of Technology and completed postdoctoral training in high-throughput imaging analysis at Northborough Research Center. Her group builds scalable, explainable tools for biological data and collaborates closely with experimental neuroscience labs.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="section muted" aria-labelledby="research-title">
        <div class="container">
          <div class="section-heading">
            <p class="eyebrow">Research Interests</p>
            <h2 id="research-title">Research themes</h2>
          </div>
          <div class="card-grid">
            <article class="card">
              <h3>Neural Encoding &amp; Decoding</h3>
              <p>Developing interpretable models that translate spike-train data into behavioral predictions.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
              <h3>Biomedical Imaging</h3>
              <p>Applying convolutional and graph neural networks to magnetic resonance and two-photon microscopy data.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
              <h3>Single-Cell Omics</h3>
              <p>Designing scalable pipelines for integrating multimodal single-cell genomics and spatial transcriptomics.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="card">
              <h3>Explainable AI</h3>
              <p>Building frameworks to probe decision boundaries and feature attributions in black-box models.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section container" aria-labelledby="projects-title">
        <div class="section-heading">
          <p class="eyebrow">Selected Projects</p>
          <h2 id="projects-title">Current and recent work</h2>
        </div>
        <div class="timeline">
          <article>
            <h3>DeepVision: High-Resolution Neural Activity Mapping</h3>
            <p><strong>Role:</strong> Lead Developer &amp; Project Coordinator</p>
            <p>Designed a PyTorch-based pipeline for two-photon image segmentation and stimulus decoding from calcium-imaging traces.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>NeuroGraph: Graph Neural Networks for Circuit Analysis</h3>
            <p><strong>Role:</strong> Principal Investigator</p>
            <p>Constructed graph representations of reconstructed neuron meshes to classify synapse types and infer connectivity motifs.</p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h3>CellMap: Multi-Modal Single-Cell Atlas</h3>
            <p><strong>Role:</strong> Co-Principal Investigator</p>
            <p>Developed a Nextflow workflow integrating scRNA-Seq, ATAC-Seq, and spatial FISH data for cortical organoid studies.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="section muted" aria-labelledby="credentials-title">
        <div class="container two-column">
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Education</p>
            <h2 id="credentials-title">Training</h2>
            <ul class="clean-list">
              <li><strong>Ph.D., Computational Biology</strong><br>Baywood Institute of Technology, 2014–2019</li>
              <li><strong>M.Sc., Bioinformatics</strong><br>Riverbend University, 2012–2014</li>
              <li><strong>B.Sc., Computer Science</strong><br>Crestfield College of Engineering, 2008–2012</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="eyebrow">Teaching &amp; Tools</p>
            <h2>Mentorship and skills</h2>
            <p>Dr. Moreno teaches computational neuroscience and advanced machine learning methods in biology, and has supervised 8 Ph.D. students and 12 Master’s theses.</p>
            <p><strong>Tools:</strong> Python, R, C++, PyTorch, TensorFlow, scikit-learn, NetworkX, Nextflow, Snakemake, Docker, Kubernetes, MATLAB, Jupyter, Seurat, Scanpy, D3.js, Plotly, Matplotlib.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>
