            <p class="eyebrow">March 2025</p>
            <h2>Building Interpretable Deep Learning Models for Neuroscience</h2>
            <p>Interpretable neural decoders require more than strong predictive performance. Our lab evaluates feature attributions, stability across recording sessions, and alignment with known circuit physiology before using models to generate hypotheses.</p>
          </article>
          <article id="single-cell-genomics" class="feature-article">
            <p class="eyebrow">January 2025</p>
            <h2>Bridging Machine Learning and Single-Cell Genomics</h2>
            <p>Single-cell projects succeed when data engineering, statistical modeling, and biological interpretation are designed together. CellMap reflects this by combining reproducible workflows with Bayesian clustering and careful visual review.</p>
          </article>
          <article id="connectomics" class="feature-article">
            <p class="eyebrow">November 2024</p>
            <h2>Scaling Graph Neural Networks for Connectomics</h2>
            <p>Connectomics graphs are large, noisy, and richly structured. NeuroGraph focuses on robust graph representations that help researchers classify synapses and compare connectivity motifs across datasets.</p>
          </article>
        </div>
